}

::ENG1_U01_L05_Q15::[MLA.ENG1.L.01] Passage: The museum offered audio guides. Visitors listened to explanations while viewing exhibits. Question: Which response uses correct conventions?{
~A. The audio guides helped visitors they listened to explanations.#Incorrect. This is a run-on.
~B. the audio guides helped visitors listen to explanations.#Incorrect. The first word needs capitalization.
