~D. Because visitors listened to explanations while viewing exhibits.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
}

::ENG1_U01_L05_Q16::[MLA.ENG1.L.01] Passage: The teacher highlighted project due dates. Students knew when notes, drafts, and final copies were due. Question: Which sentence uses commas correctly?{
~A. Students knew when notes drafts and final copies were due.#Incorrect. The list needs commas after notes and drafts.
=B. Students knew when notes, drafts, and final copies were due.#Correct. The commas separate the items in the list clearly.
~C. Students knew, when notes, drafts, and final copies were due.#Incorrect. The first comma is unnecessary and interrupts the sentence.
~D. Students knew when, notes drafts and final copies were due.#Incorrect. The comma after when is incorrect and the list still needs commas.
}

::ENG1_U01_L05_Q17::[MLA.ENG1.L.01] Passage: The shelter posted lost-pet photos online. Owners checked the photos before driving to the shelter. Question: Which response is correct?{
