~C. Owners checked the online photos before driving to the shelter#Incorrect. The sentence needs end punctuation.
~D. Because owners checked the online photos.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
}

::ENG1_U01_L05_Q18::[MLA.ENG1.L.01] Passage: The community garden labeled plant rows. Visitors knew which vegetables were growing. Question: Which sentence fixes the run-on "The labels helped visitors they knew which vegetables were growing"?{
~A. The labels helped visitors, they knew which vegetables were growing.#Incorrect. This is a comma splice.
=B. The labels helped visitors know which vegetables were growing.#Correct. This is one complete sentence with correct sentence boundaries.
~C. Because the labels helped visitors know vegetables.#Incorrect. This is a fragment and is not specific enough.
~D. the labels helped visitors know which vegetables were growing#Incorrect. This lacks capitalization and punctuation.
}

